//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// H-007 · Cross-sectional crypto ranking  —  board score 2.9/10  —  REJECTED
// prop_lab · https://github.com/KristijonasSim/prop_lab
//
// DO NOT TRADE THIS. Kept because HOW it failed is the useful part.
//
// WHY IT WAS REJECTED — and this one is different from the others. The ranking
// CARRIES REAL INFORMATION: before costs, 95.0% of the 360 real configurations
// beat PF 1.0 against the paired null's 59.4% (median 1.096 vs 1.009). That is a
// cleaner separation from the null than H-003 or H-005 ever managed.
//
// It still fails, because the edge is worth about 10% on profit factor and a
// 14bps round trip is worth more than that. Median PF by cost: 1.096 (0x) ->
// 0.825 (1x) -> 0.618 (2x). Every configuration that cleared the gate at 2x was
// a 1-day bar held 7 days, 0.14 trades/day, with 400-875 days to target against
// H-002's 25. Walk-forward: 1.168, and 1.063 at 2x — under the gate, with the
// best of five null seeds at 1.065 BEATING it.
//
// COST-LIMITED, NOT SIGNAL-LIMITED. That matters: a signal that loses to its
// null is dead, but one that loses to the spread gets better with a wider
// universe, because cross-sectional dispersion grows with the number of names
// ranked while the cost per trade does not. The published versions rank 500 to
// 7,000 names. This ranks five, which is why it is closer to a coin-flip on
// dispersion than to the real mechanic.
//
// Add symbols in the inputs to test that directly — it is the one open route.
// =============================================================================
//
// THIS IS THE INDICATOR TWIN, generated by pine/build_indicators.py from the
// strategy of the same name. Identical levels, filters and entry conditions;
// no orders, no exits, no Strategy Tester numbers. Use the strategy version
// when you want to check our backtest, this one when you want it on a chart.
// Exits are part of the edge and they are NOT shown here - a chart full of
// entry arrows says nothing about what happens after the entry.
indicator("H-007 Cross-sectional ranking · signals · prop_lab [REJECTED]", overlay=false)

sig   = input.string("momentum", "Ranking signal", options=["momentum","relative volume"],
     tooltip="momentum = L-bar log return. relative volume = volume over its own " +
             "rolling median, which is the signal the published equity version uses.")
L     = input.int(6,  "Lookback (bars)", minval=1)
mode  = input.string("spread", "Book", options=["spread","long only"],
     tooltip="spread = long the top name, short the bottom. long only = top name only.")
holdB = input.int(7,  "Hold (bars)", minval=1,
     tooltip="Everything that survived cost in the study was a 7-day hold on 1d bars.")

s1 = input.symbol("BINANCE:BTCUSDT", "Coin 1")
s2 = input.symbol("BINANCE:ETHUSDT", "Coin 2")
s3 = input.symbol("BINANCE:SOLUSDT", "Coin 3")
s4 = input.symbol("BINANCE:BNBUSDT", "Coin 4")
s5 = input.symbol("BINANCE:XRPUSDT", "Coin 5")

score(sym) =>
    [c, vv] = request.security(sym, timeframe.period, [close, volume], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
    m  = math.log(c / c[L])
    md = ta.median(vv, L)
    sig == "momentum" ? m : (md > 0 ? vv / md : na)

r1 = score(s1)
r2 = score(s2)
r3 = score(s3)
r4 = score(s4)
r5 = score(s5)

// rank the current chart symbol against the five, on the same measure
own    = sig == "momentum" ? math.log(close / close[L]) :
         (ta.median(volume, L) > 0 ? volume / ta.median(volume, L) : na)
best   = math.max(r1, r2, r3, r4, r5)
worst  = math.min(r1, r2, r3, r4, r5)
isTop  = not na(own) and not na(best)  and own >= best
isBot  = not na(own) and not na(worst) and own <= worst

ready = barstate.isconfirmed and not na(own)
plot(own, "This symbol", color.new(color.orange, 0), 2)
plot(best,  "Best of set",  color.new(color.green, 40))
plot(worst, "Worst of set", color.new(color.red, 40))
hline(0, "", color.new(color.gray, 60))

// ------------------------------------------------------- signals & alerts ---
// The same two conditions the strategy enters on, drawn instead of traded.
longSignal_  = ready and isTop
shortSignal_ = ready and isBot and mode == "spread"
plotshape(longSignal_,  "Long signal",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar,
     color.new(color.green, 0), size=size.small)
plotshape(shortSignal_, "Short signal", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar,
     color.new(color.red, 0),   size=size.small)
alertcondition(longSignal_,  "H-007 Cross-sectional ranking long",  "H-007 Cross-sectional ranking: long signal on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(shortSignal_, "H-007 Cross-sectional ranking short", "H-007 Cross-sectional ranking: short signal on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
